od/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java:189-227`: the schema definitions for `encounters` (`EncounterGet`, `EncounterGetRef`, `EncounterCreate`). These are documentation, not the serialization path, so they are included for completeness only.\n\n**What I could not establish:**\n- The commit SHA and PR that introduced the change. `RESTWS-1037` has no matches in any repository in Falkon, and I had no tool that lists commits.\n- The pre-fix code. I read only the current `VisitResource1_9.java` and its test.\n- The privilege aspect in the question. Nothing in these files checks encounter privileges when serializing visit encounters, so the access behavior probably comes from the encounter service or the resource's privilege handling. I did not check that code.\n\nTo settle it, search the module's commit history for `RESTWS-1037` (for example `git log --all --grep=RESTWS-1037 -- omod/src/main/java/.../VisitResource1_9.java`) and read the diff of `getNonVoidedEncounters` in that commit.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java\", \"startLine\": 130, \"endLine\": 143},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java\", \"startLine\": 99, \"endLine\": 99},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java\", \"startLine\": 83, \"endLine\": 83},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/test/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9Test.java\", \"startLine\": 36, \"endLine\": 63},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResourc